[6] Proof readout
  The lift makes the q=3 unital useful in exactly the conservative sense:
    it supplies pair-unique 4-point completions for marked C27 transfer
    pairs after AP/GW labels are attached.
  It does not canonically identify the unital with AP8 pair slots.
  New local target:
    show that any low-gap non-AP/GW residual must lift to either the
    AP/GW anchor block, a unit-petal block, or the three-block
    AP/GW--near/K33--petal chain.  Then route the unit block to C27
    petal/two-swap discharge and the nonunit chain to HYP-2908.
  POKE contribution:
    treat q=3 unital blocks as a pair-completion forum for transfer
    packets, not as scalar evidence or a canonical AP8 design.
